{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01VsCQdRgcCLa8pcgLHJNNpV", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diocese_of_San_Jose_de_Antique\"}, {\"url\": \"https://catholic-hierarchy.org/diocese/dsjda.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://mail.catholic-hierarchy.org/diocese/dsjda.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://heraldry-wiki.com/wiki/Diocese_of_San_Jose_de_Antique\"}, {\"url\": \"https://gcatholic.org/dioceses/diocese/zjos3.htm?tab=stat\"}, {\"url\": \"https://philippines123.com/wiki/Saint_Joseph_Cathedral_(Antique)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://gcatholic.org/dioceses/diocese/zjos3.htm\"}, {\"url\": \"https://stmariagoretti.archtoronto.org/en/parish-life/parish-blog/parish/bishops-visit\"}, {\"url\": \"https://stmariagoretti.archtoronto.org/pl/parish-life/parish-blog/parish/bishops-visit/\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:47:02.936Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Diocese of San Jose de Antique erected", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_017GZsurNreaKkJpRvdmBSGb", "content": [{"title": "Diocese of San Jose de Antique", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diocese_of_San_Jose_de_Antique"}, {"title": "Catholic-Hierarchy DC", "url": "https://catholic-hierarchy.org/diocese/dsjda.html"}, {"title": "Catholic-Hierarchy DC", "url": "https://mail.catholic-hierarchy.org/diocese/dsjda.html"}, {"title": "Diocese of San Jose de Antique", "url": "https://heraldry-wiki.com/wiki/Diocese_of_San_Jose_de_Antique"}, {"title": "Diocese of", "url": "https://gcatholic.org/dioceses/diocese/zjos3.htm?tab=stat"}, {"title": "Saint Joseph Cathedral (Antique)", "url": "https://philippines123.com/wiki/Saint_Joseph_Cathedral_(Antique)"}, {"title": "Diocese of", "url": "https://gcatholic.org/dioceses/diocese/zjos3.htm"}, {"title": "bishops visit", "url": "https://stmariagoretti.archtoronto.org/en/parish-life/parish-blog/parish/bishops-visit"}, {"title": "bishops visit", "url": "https://stmariagoretti.archtoronto.org/pl/parish-life/parish-blog/parish/bishops-visit/"}]}, "The Diocese of San Jose de Antique began as a territorial prelature in 1962 and became a diocese in 1982. The sources disagree on the exact 1962 date.\n\n- **Wikipedia** gives June 18, 1962 as the date Pope John XXIII set up the prelature, carved out of the Archdiocese of Jaro. On June 18, 1962, Pope John XXIII erected the Territorial Prelature of San Jose de Antique with the Apostolic Constitution \"Novae cuiusque Ecclesiae constitutio\". The new territorial prelature was separated from the Archdiocese of Jaro comprising the whole province of Antique\n- **Catholic-Hierarchy** lists 24 March 1962 as the erection date, and 15 November 1982 as the date it was elevated to a diocese.\n- **Heraldry-wiki** agrees on 1962 as the founding year and 1982 as the elevation year.\n\nThe diocese now covers the whole province of Antique, and its cathedral is in San Jose de Buenavista. The current bishop is Marvyn Maceda, who took office in January 2019 according to gcatholic.org."], "durationSeconds": 5.148199666999997, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01VsCQdRgcCLa8pcgLHJNNpV", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01Pvdg9PAxSqyFfxUc4C1wd7", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diocese_of_San_Jose_(Nueva_Ecija)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Joseph_Cathedral_(Nueva_Ecija)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://heraldry-wiki.com/wiki/Diocese_of_San_Jose_in_Nueva_Ecija\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.ucanews.com/directory/dioceses/philippines-san-jose-nueva-ecija/407\"}, {\"url\": \"https://partnernews.mambu.com/default.aspx/B13U0N/999564/Diocese\"}, {\"url\": \"https://goodhome.co.ke/^99423794/bhesitates/icelebratev/rintervenef/san+jose+santo.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://philippines123.com/wiki/Saint_Joseph_Cathedral_(Nueva_Ecija)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://dev.studyabroadfoundation.org/default.aspx/B13U0N/999564/Diocese\"}, {\"url\": \"https://gcatholic.org/dioceses/diocese/zjos1.htm?tab=stat\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:47:04.459Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Diocese of San Jose Nueva Ecija erected 1984", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01SfpvDA98ychNjDEZ8KPJXp", "content": [{"title": "Diocese of San Jose (Nueva Ecija)", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diocese_of_San_Jose_(Nueva_Ecija)"}, {"title": "Saint Joseph Cathedral (Nueva Ecija)", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Joseph_Cathedral_(Nueva_Ecija)"}, {"title": "Diocese of San Jose in Nueva Ecija", "url": "https://heraldry-wiki.com/wiki/Diocese_of_San_Jose_in_Nueva_Ecija"}, {"title": "Support Asian Catholic Dioceses Directory", "url": "https://www.ucanews.com/directory/dioceses/philippines-san-jose-nueva-ecija/407"}, {"title": "Diocese Of San Jose Nueva Ecija", "url": "https://partnernews.mambu.com/default.aspx/B13U0N/999564/Diocese Of San Jose Nueva Ecija.pdf"}, {"title": "goodhome.co.ke", "url": "https://goodhome.co.ke/^99423794/bhesitates/icelebratev/rintervenef/san+jose+santo.pdf"}, {"title": "Saint Joseph Cathedral (Nueva Ecija)", "url": "https://philippines123.com/wiki/Saint_Joseph_Cathedral_(Nueva_Ecija)"}, {"title": "Diocese Of San Jose Nueva Ecija", "url": "https://dev.studyabroadfoundation.org/default.aspx/B13U0N/999564/Diocese Of San Jose Nueva Ecija.pdf"}, {"title": "Diocese of", "url": "https://gcatholic.org/dioceses/diocese/zjos1.htm?tab=stat"}]}, "The sources agree the diocese was erected in 1984, but they disagree on the exact dates.\n\n- **Establishment date:** Wikipedia says Pope John Paul II established it on February 16, 1984, through the papal bull *Saepe Catholicorum Utilitas*. The Diocese of San Jose, located in Nueva Ecija, Philippines, was established by Pope John Paul II on February 16, 1984 by virtue of the papal bull Saepe Catholicorum Utilitas. UCA News gives the same February 16 date. The Diocese of San Jose, Nueva Ecija, was created on Feb. 16, 1984 by Pope John Paul II and canonically erected on July 14, 1984.\n- **Canonical erection:** Wikipedia and UCA News both put this on July 14, 1984. Wikipedia adds that the diocese is a suffragan of the Archdiocese of Lingayen–Dagupan.\n- **Outliers:** Two PDF documents give June 16, 1984 and June 4, 1984 (via the papal bull \"Quod Christus\"). These look less reliable, since they conflict with the other sources and the PDFs appear to be low-quality copies.\n- **Origin:** The diocese was carved out of the Diocese of Cabanatuan. Sixteen parishes, out of 41 parishes of the Diocese of Cabanatuan were adjudicated to the Diocese of San Jose, Nueva Ecija.\n- **First bishop:** UCA News says Bishop Florentino F. Cinense, DD, was appointed the diocese's first residential bishop on July 14, 1984. The PDFs name Bishop Leo Drona as the first bishop, but UCA News and gcatholic.org indicate Drona succeeded Cinense in 1987, so the PDFs appear to be wrong on this point.\n- **Cathedral:** Saint Joseph Cathedral became the cathedral of the Diocese of San Jose whose territory comprises the northern half of the province in 1984.\n\nThe best-supported answer is a February 16, 1984 establishment and a July 14, 1984 canonical erection."], "durationSeconds": 7.148189125000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Pvdg9PAxSqyFfxUc4C1wd7", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
